# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=FileX
Version=v1.0.0_H5_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
FX_DISABLE_DIRECT_DATA_READ_CACHE_FILL|FX_DISABLE_DIRECT_DATA_READ_CACHE_FILL|Core||||Direct read sector cache will be disabled if cache is disabled.
FX_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|FX_DISABLE_ERROR_CHECKING|Core||||Removes the basic FileX error checking API and results in improved performance (as much as 30%) and smaller code size.
FX_DONT_UPDATE_OPEN_FILES|FX_DONT_UPDATE_OPEN_FILES|Core||||Defined, FileX does not update already opened files
FX_ENABLE_EXFAT|FX_ENABLE_EXFAT|Core||||Defined, FileX is able to access exFAT file system.
FX_ENABLE_FAULT_TOLERANT|FX_ENABLE_FAULT_TOLERANT|Core||||Defined, enables FileX fault tolerant service.
FX_FAT_MAP_SIZE|FX_FAT_MAP_SIZE|Core||1|16777215|Specifies the number of sectors that can be represented in the FAT update map. The default value is 256, but this can be overridden with a command-line define. Larger values help reduce unneeded updates of secondary FAT sectors.
FX_FAULT_TOLERANT|FX_FAULT_TOLERANT|Core||||Defined, system sector write requests (including FAT and directory entry requests) are flushed immediately to the driver.
FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_BOOT_INDEX|FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_BOOT_INDEX|Core||0|2147483647|Define byte offset in boot sector where the cluster number of the Fault Tolerant Log file is.
FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_DATA|FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_DATA|Core||||Defined, data sector write requests are flushed immediately to the driver.
FX_MAX_FAT_CACHE|FX_MAX_FAT_CACHE|Core||||Specifies the number of entries in the internal FAT cache. The default value is 16, but this can be overridden with a command-line define. All values must be a power of 2.
FX_MAX_LAST_NAME_LEN|FX_MAX_LAST_NAME_LEN|Core||13|256|This value defines the maximum file name length, which includes full path name. FX_MAX_LAST_NAME_LEN must be as large or larger than FX_MAX_LONG_NAME_LEN
FX_MAX_LONG_NAME_LEN|FX_MAX_LONG_NAME_LEN|Core||13|256|Defines the maximum size of long file names supported by FileX.
FX_MAX_SECTOR_CACHE|FX_MAX_SECTOR_CACHE|Core||||Defines the maximum number of logical sectors that can be cached by FileX. The cache memory supplied to FileX at fx_media_open determines how many sectors can actually be cached The FX_MAX_SECTOR_CACHE is 2 to the power of MAX_SECTOR_CACHE_NB_BIT.
FX_MEDIA_DISABLE_SEARCH_CACHE|FX_MEDIA_DISABLE_SEARCH_CACHE|Core||||Defined, the file search cache optimization is disabled.
FX_MEDIA_STATISTICS_DISABLE|FX_MEDIA_STATISTICS_DISABLE|Core||||Defined, gathering of media statistics is disabled.
FX_NO_LOCAL_PATH|FX_NO_LOCAL_PATH|Core||||Defined, local path logic is disabled.
FX_NO_TIMER|FX_NO_TIMER|Core||||Eliminates the ThreadX timer setup to update the FileX system time and date. Doing so causes default time and date to be placed on all file operations.
FX_RENAME_PATH_INHERIT|FX_RENAME_PATH_INHERIT|Core||||Defined, renaming inherits path information.
FX_SINGLE_OPEN_LEGACY|FX_SINGLE_OPEN_LEGACY|Core||||Defined, legacy single open logic for the same file is enabled.
FX_SINGLE_THREAD|FX_SINGLE_THREAD|Core||||Eliminates ThreadX protection logic from the FileX source. It should be used if FileX is being used only from one thread or if FileX is being used without ThreadX.
FX_UPDATE_RATE_IN_SECONDS|FX_UPDATE_RATE_IN_SECONDS|Core||0|65535|Defines the number of seconds the time parameters are updated in FileX.
FX_UPDATE_RATE_IN_TICKS|FX_UPDATE_RATE_IN_TICKS|Core||||Defines the number of ThreadX timer ticks required to achieve the update rate. That is, the update rate, but in ticks.
FileX_Version|FileX version|Version||||FileX version
MAX_FAT_CACHE_NB_BIT|MAX_FAT_CACHE_NB_BIT|Core||3|10|Represents the power of which FX_MAX_FAT_CACHE is rised to
MAX_SECTOR_CACHE_NB_BIT|MAX_SECTOR_CACHE_NB_BIT|Core||1|10|represents the power of which FX_MAX_SECTOR_CACHE is rised to
FX_DRIVER_USE_64BIT_LBA|FX_DRIVER_USE_64BIT_LBA|Core||||Defined, enables 64-bits sector addresses used in I/O driver.
FX_SRAM_BASE_ADDRESS_RANGES|SRAM Disk Address ranges|SRAM Disk||||define the address range from which the SRAM file system will be created
FX_SRAM_BASE_ADDRESS|SRAM Disk Address|SRAM Disk||0x20120000|0x20180000|define the address from which the SRAM file system will be created
SRAM_DISK_SIZE|SRAM Disk Size|SRAM Disk||2048|393216|define the SRAM file system disk size: 16K
SD_SECTOR_SIZE|Default Sector Size|SD Driver||512|4096|define the default sector size, needed by the fx_media_format() API.
ENABLE_CACHE_MAINTENANCE|Enable data cache maintenance|SD Driver||||When using cachable memory region, it is recommended to maintain the data cache to always ensure data integrity between CPU and SD DMA operations.
SDMMC_INSTANCE|SD instance|SD Driver||||define the default SD instance to use.
FX_DRIVER_SDMMC_INIT|FX Driver Initializes the SD IP|SD Driver||||by default, the FX SD driver initializes the SD IP, set this flag to false to let the application do the init.
GLUE_FUNCTIONS|Glue Function Implementation|SD Driver||||
TRANSFER_NOTIFICATION|Transfer Completion Mechanism|SD Driver||||
MMC_SECTOR_SIZE|Default Sector Size|MMC Driver||512|4096|define the default sector size, needed by the fx_media_format() API.
MMC_ENABLE_CACHE_MAINTENANCE|Enable data cache maintenance|MMC Driver||||When using cachable memory region, it is recommended to maintain the data cache to always ensure data integrity between CPU and SD DMA operations.
MMC_INSTANCE|MMC instance|MMC Driver||||define the default SD instance to use.
FX_DRIVER_MMC_INIT|FX Driver Initializes the MMC IP|MMC Driver||||by default, the FX SDMMC driver initializes the SDMMC IP, set this flag to false to let the application do the init.
MMC_GLUE_FUNCTIONS|Glue Function Implementation|MMC Driver||||
MMC_TRANSFER_NOTIFICATION|Transfer Completion Mechanism|MMC Driver||||
ULONG_64_DEFINED|ULONG64 TYPE|Core||||the default value of the ULONG64 type
FX_LX_NOR_CUSTOM_DRIVER_NAME|FX_LX_NOR_CUSTOM_DRIVER_NAME|NOR Custom driver||||define the NOR custom driver name.
FX_LX_NOR_CUSTOM_DRIVER_ID|FX_LX_NOR_CUSTOM_DRIVER_ID|NOR Custom driver||0|0xFFFFFFFE|Define the NOR custom driver id. The value of FX_LX_NOR_CUSTOM_DRIVER_ID should not take the value of the UNKNOWN_DRIVER_ID that is 0xFFFFFFFF
FX_LX_NOR_CUSTOM_DRIVER_INIT|FX_LX_NOR_CUSTOM_DRIVER_INIT|NOR Custom driver||||define the NOR custom driver initialization function.
LX_NOR_USE_CUSTOM_DRIVER|LX_NOR_USE_CUSTOM_DRIVER|Custom driver||||
LX_NOR_USE_SIMULATOR_DRIVER|LX_NOR_USE_SIMULATOR_DRIVER|Custom driver||||
LX_NOR_USE_OSPI_DRIVER|LX_NOR_USE_OSPI_DRIVER|Custom driver||||
FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER_NAME|FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER_NAME|NAND Custom driver||||define the NAND custom driver name.
FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER_ID|FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER_ID|NAND Custom driver||0|0xFFFFFFFE|define the NAND custom driver id. The value of FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER_ID should not take the value of the UNKNOWN_DRIVER_ID that is 0xFFFFFFFF
FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER_INIT|FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER_INIT|NAND Custom driver||||define the NAND custom driver initialization function.
LX_NAND_USE_CUSTOM_DRIVER|LX_NAND_USE_CUSTOM_DRIVER|Custom driver||||
LX_NAND_USE_SIMULATOR_DRIVER|LX_NAND_USE_SIMULATOR_DRIVER|Custom driver||||
FX_APP_MEM_POOL_SIZE|FileX memory pool size|Memory Configuration||1024|262144|Default memory pool size for the FileX application.<font color="red">The allocated memory for all enabled middelwares should not exceed the total size of available memory.</font>
AZRTOS_APP_MEM_ALLOCATION_METHOD|Memory Allocation|Core||||
FX_STANDALONE_ENABLE|FX_STANDALONE_ENABLE|Core||||Configure the FileX in Standalone mode.
FX_DISABLE_CACHE|FX_DISABLE_CACHE|Core||||Determine if cache is disabled.
FX_DISABLE_FILE_CLOSE|FX_DISABLE_FILE_CLOSE|Core||||If defined, file close is disabled.
FX_DISABLE_FAST_OPEN|FX_DISABLE_FAST_OPEN|Core||||If defined, fast open is disabled.
FX_DISABLE_FORCE_MEMORY_OPERATION|FX_DISABLE_FORCE_MEMORY_OPERATION|Core||||If defined, force memory operations are disabled.
FX_DISABLE_BUILD_OPTIONS|FX_DISABLE_BUILD_OPTIONS|Core||||If defined, build options is disabled.
FX_DISABLE_ONE_LINE_FUNCTION|FX_DISABLE_ONE_LINE_FUNCTION|Core||||If defined, one line function is disabled.
FX_DISABLE_FAT_ENTRY_REFRESH|FX_DISABLE_FAT_ENTRY_REFRESH|Core||||If defined, FAT entry refresh is disabled.
FX_DISABLE_CONSECUTIVE_DETECT|FX_DISABLE_CONSECUTIVE_DETECT|Core||||If defined, consecutive detect is disabled.
FX_EXFAT_MAX_CACHE_SIZE|FX_EXFAT_MAX_CACHE_SIZE|Core||||Define bitmap cache size for exFAT. Size should be minimum one sector size and maximum 4096. For applications using multiple media devices with varying sector size, the value should be set to the size of largest sector size. The FX_EXFAT_MAX_CACHE_SIZE is 2 power of FX_EXFAT_MAX_CACHE_SIZE_NB_BIT.
FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_CACHE_SIZE|FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_CACHE_SIZE|Core||||Define the size of fault tolerant cache, which is used when freeing FAT chain. The FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_CACHE_SIZE is 2 power of FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_CACHE_SIZE_NB_SIZE.
FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_CACHE_SIZE_NB_SIZE|FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_CACHE_SIZE_NB_SIZE|Core||3|14|Represents the exponent power of which FX_FAULT_TOLERANT_CACHE_SIZE is rised to.
FX_EXFAT_MAX_CACHE_SIZE_NB_BIT|FX_EXFAT_MAX_CACHE_SIZE_NB_BIT|Core||7|12|Represents the exponent power of which FX_EXFAT_MAX_CACHE_SIZE is rised to.
FILEX_MEM_POOL_VAR_NAME|FileX MemPool Name|Memory Configuration||||Default FileX memory pool var name <font color="red"> <b>This is a variable name. It should be C compliant declaration, Otherwise compilation errors will be generated in the project. </b> </font>
GENERATE_FILEX_INIT_CODE|FileX Generate Init Code|FileX Core Init||||Generate application code to initialize the FileX/LevelX stack in MX_FileX_Init() function.
FILEX_APPLICATION_THREAD_ENTRY_NAME|FileX Application Thread Entry Name|FileX Core Init||||Main thread entry function Name.
FILEX_APPLICATION_THREAD_PRIORITY|FileX Application Thread Priority|FileX Core Init||0|31|FileX Application Thread Priority value for FileX application.
FILEX_APPLICATION_THREAD_STACK_SIZE|FileX Application Thread Stack Size.|FileX Core Init||512|262144|Thread stack size value for FileX application. <font color="red">The allocated memory for all enabled middelwares should not exceed the total size of available memory.</font>
LINK_SRAM_DRIVER|Link SRAM Driver|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_open() function call to link the SRAM Driver to the application.
FORMAT_SRAM_MEDIA|Format SRAM Media|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_format() function call to format the SRAM Media.
LINK_SD_DRIVER|Link SD Driver|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_open() function call to link the SD Driver to the application.
FORMAT_SD_MEDIA|Format SD Media|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_format() function call to format the SD Media.
LINK_MMC_DRIVER|Link MMC Driver|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_open() function call to link the MMC Driver to the application.
FORMAT_MMC_MEDIA|Format MMC Media|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_format() function call to format the MMC Media.
LINK_NOR_OSPI_DRIVER|Link NOR OSPI Driver|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_open() function call to link the NOR OSPI Driver to the application.
FORMAT_NOR_OSPI_MEDIA|Format NOR OSPI Media|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_open() function call to link the NOR OSPI Driver to the application.
LINK_NOR_SIMULATOR_DRIVER|Link NOR SIMULATOR Driver|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_open() function call to link the NOR SIMULATOR Driver to the application.
FORMAT_NOR_SIMULATOR_MEDIA|Format NOR SIMULATOR Media|FileX Drivers||||Generates fx_media_format() function call to format the NOR SIMULATOR Media.
FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER|FX_LX_NAND_CUSTOM_DRIVER|NAND Custom driver||||define the NAND custom driver initialization function.

